# Patches that Apex applies to Fedora's libfprint, in order.
#
# Format (parsed by build.sh):
# - One patch file name per line, relative to packaging/libfprint/patches/,
#   named NNNN-short-name.patch. No paths, no spaces, no duplicates.
# - Patches are applied in the order listed, each on top of the ones before
#   it. build.sh adds them to Fedora's libfprint.spec as Patch1001,
#   Patch1002, ... and the spec's `%autosetup -S git` applies each one with
#   `git apply --index`, which allows no fuzz.
# - '#' starts a comment that runs to the end of the line. Blank lines are
#   ignored.
# - A patch in patches/ that is not listed here is never applied.
#
# Numbering:
# - 00xx: enabled fixes. Only 00xx patches may be listed here.
# - 01xx: carried but disabled. They stay in patches/, rebased so that each
#   one applies on top of the listed 00xx patches. build.sh refuses an 01xx
#   name here. To enable one, attach the debug log lines that show its
#   trigger (patches/README.md names them), `git mv` it to the next free
#   00xx number and add that name below.
#
# If a listed patch stops applying, the image ships Fedora's stock libfprint
# and is labelled degraded=fingerprint (ADR 0006). Most likely upstream has
# merged or changed the fix, so check that before rebasing.
